(Phases of Database Design) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 416.69314960629913 Td
(Database design typically follows a structured lifecycle, moving from high-level requirements to detailed) Tj
T* (physical implementation.) Tj
T* (- **Requirements Analysis**: Understanding the user needs, business rules, and expected data usage. This) Tj
T* (involves interviews, surveys, and documentation review.) Tj
T* (- **Conceptual Design**: Creating a high-level data model, independent of any specific DBMS.) Tj
T* (Entity-Relationship Diagrams \(ERDs\) are commonly used here. Focuses on 'what' data to store.) Tj
T* (- **Logical Design**: Translating the conceptual model into a data model specific to the chosen DBMS \(e.g.,) Tj
T* (relational, object-oriented\). This involves defining tables, columns, primary keys, foreign keys, and) Tj
T* (relationships. Focuses on 'how' data is structured logically.) Tj
T* (- **Physical Design**: Detailing the actual implementation of the database, including storage structures,) Tj
T* (indexing strategies, partitioning, and security measures. Optimizing for performance and storage. Focuses on) Tj
T* ('how' data is stored physically.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 14 Tf
16.0999999999999979 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 189.9214960629919915 Td
(Data Modeling, ERDs, and Normalization) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
11.5 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 161.5750393700786844 Td
(**Data Modeling** is the process of creating a visual representation of either a whole information system or) Tj
T* (parts of it to communicate connections between data points and structures.) Tj
T* (- **Entity-Relationship Diagrams \(ERDs\)** are graphical tools used in conceptual data modeling to represent) Tj
T* (entities, their attributes, and relationships between them.) Tj
T* (    - **Entity**: A real-world object or concept \(e.g., Student, Course\).) Tj
T* (    - **Attribute**: A property or characteristic of an entity \(e.g., StudentID, CourseName\).) Tj
T* (    - **Relationship**: An association between two or more entities \(e.g., a Student *enrolls in* a Course\).) Tj
T* (- **Normalization** is a systematic process of organizing the columns and tables of a relational database to) Tj
T* (minimize data redundancy and improve data integrity. It aims to eliminate undesirable characteristics like) Tj
T* (insertion, update, and deletion anomalies.) Tj
T* (- Common Normal Forms include 1NF, 2NF, 3NF, and BCNF, each building upon the previous one with stricter) Tj
T* (rules.) Tj
ET
