/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 773.8585039370078675 Td
(Second Normal Form \(2NF\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0 g
170.0787401574803255 773.8585039370078675 Td
(Must be in 1NF AND all non-key attributes must be fully functionally dependent on the primary key.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0 g
283.4645669291338663 773.8585039370078675 Td
(Reduces redundancy for composite primary keys.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0 g
56.6929133858267775 762.5199212598424765 Td
(Third Normal Form \(3NF\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0 g
170.0787401574803255 762.5199212598424765 Td
(Must be in 2NF AND eliminate transitive dependencies \(non-key attributes should not depend on other non-key attributes\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0 g
283.4645669291338663 762.5199212598424765 Td
(Significantly reduces data redundancy and update anomalies.) Tj
ET
